&nbsp;


Occupational Sick Pay (OSP)




Your contract makes it clear that absence and any entitlement to pay is subject to the firm’s sickness policy. That policy is not contractual and we are not obliged to inform you of the content. Employees are expected to review policies which are in place from
 time to time and are available on HiBob. The applicable policy was in place (and available for you to review) prior to your current period of sick leave and governs your entitlement to OSP and SSP.




The sickness policy uploaded on 17 November 2025 was the first version of a formal policy. There was no previous written sickness policy in place.




OSP condition 7(5) was included in this first version. The policy was published to clarify eligibility for occupational sick pay going forward for all staff, including those under notice of resignation.




The firm confirms that there is no employee currently working their notice who is in receipt of OSP, since the introduction of this policy.&nbsp;




Please note we have made our position clear on your entitlement to sick pay and will not be engaging in any further correspondence with you on this matter. &nbsp;


